> f8(x: i8, y: i8) = (x+y)^2
> g8(x: i8, y: i8) = x^2 + 2*x*y + y^2
> equiv f8 g8
f8 and g8 are equal on the domain of f8 (exhaustive)
> f(x: real, y: real) = (x+y)^2
> g(x: real, y: real) = x^2 + 2*x*y + y^2
> equiv f g
f and g differ at 529504 points, e.g. x=-9.98, y=-10: 399.2 vs 399.2
> h(x: real, y: real) = x^2 + y^2
> equiv f h
f and h differ at 1000000 points, e.g. x=-10, y=-10: 400 vs 200
> p(x: real) = (x^2-1)/(x-1)
> q(x: real) = x+1
> equiv p q
p and q differ at 149 points, e.g. x=-8.98: -7.98 vs -7.98
> fi(x: int, y: int) = (x+y)^2
> gi(x: int, y: int) = x^2 + 2*x*y + y^2
> equiv fi gi
fi and gi differ at 1 point of the sample, e.g. x=-9223372036854775808, y=9223372036854775806: 4 vs undefined
